// E2E protocol coverage for a release console built with
// `[release] include-compiler = true` (ADR 0125 §1.5/§1.6, BT-3575). Run
// against its own dedicated release-mode node
// (`e2e_release_mode_console_include_compiler_tests`), never the shared
// workspace-mode node `e2e_language_tests` uses.
//
// `eval` passes the protocol op gate here (`include_compiler => true`), so
// this is the file that reaches the *workspace*-row refusals
// (`Workspace flush` / `removeFromSystem`, `release_mode_no_workspace`) —
// `permitted(workspace, _Caps) -> false` unconditionally, even with
// `include-compiler` (ADR 0125 §1.5: "a release has no working tree to
// flush to"). It also proves the literal ADR 0125 §1.1/§1.8 example,
// `Beamtalk releaseInfo`, works through ordinary `eval` once a compiler is
// present — on top of the always-available `run-entry` path the default
// (no-compiler) fixture exercises instead
// (`release_console_default.btscript`).

// @load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/counter.bt

// ===========================================================================
// eval works — the compiler is present
// ===========================================================================

1 + 1
// => 2

// ===========================================================================
// Workspace ops are still refused — release_mode_no_workspace, even here
// ===========================================================================

:flush
// => ERROR: no working tree

// `Counter` (loaded above) must resolve to a real class first — an eval
// expression sends `removeFromSystem` to whatever `Counter` evaluates to,
// unlike the direct-by-name Erlang entry point
// `beamtalk_release_mode_refusal_tests:
// remove_from_system_refused_in_both_release_variants_test_` exercises,
// which the capability gate refuses before any class lookup even for a
// name that resolves to nothing.
:remove-class Counter
// => ERROR: no working tree

// ===========================================================================
// Beamtalk releaseInfo / shapeManifest — reachable through eval too
// ===========================================================================

Beamtalk releaseInfo
// => _

Beamtalk shapeManifest
// => _

BeamtalkInterface releaseInfo
// => _

BeamtalkInterface shapeManifest
// => _
